---
import Docs from '@/layouts/docs.astro';
---
<Docs title="Local development">
  <div class="doc-title">
    <span class="section-kicker">CONTRIBUTE / SETUP</span>
    <h1>One clean checkout.</h1>
    <p>Use the same pinned Rust, Node, pnpm, and container workflow as CI.</p>
  </div>
  <h2>Bootstrap</h2>
  <p>Install Rust 1.89, Node.js 22.19.0, and <code>protoc</code>, then run <code>./scripts/setup.sh</code>. It installs the Rust components and dependencies for both the root workspace and separate site workspace. The server stubs use vendored <code>protoc</code>, but the optional SPIFFE feature and protobuf descriptor check require a system compiler; set <code>PROTOC</code> to its executable path when it is not on <code>PATH</code>. The script uses Corepack when available and otherwise invokes pinned pnpm 11.22.0 through npm (or uses an already-installed pnpm 11.22.0):</p>
  <pre><code>./scripts/setup.sh</code></pre>
  <h2>Daily checks</h2>
  <pre><code>cargo test --workspace
pnpm check
pnpm build</code></pre>
  <p>Keep credentials, chain secrets, delegation keys, and audit data out of Git. The <a href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/blob/master/docs/local-development.md">repository guide ↗</a> documents the clean architecture boundaries.</p>
</Docs>
